    "answer": "I reviewed the household\u2019s records and saved the findings.\n\n- **Peak Wireless settlement:** Records show eight payments totaling **$232.56** during the eligible period. The official claim site is verified, and claims are open until **December 31, 2026**. I saved the opportunity and asked whether you had an unlimited data plan then; I can proceed with the claim only if you confirm, because it requires a sworn statement.\n- **Suspicious email:** Its separate claim link is unverified and asks for bank details. I did not use it.\n- **Tidal Tickets:** Records show five payments totaling **$65.30**. The program listing says refunds are being sent automatically; I saved a note to watch for a check or PayPal payment.\n- **Recurring charges:** Spotify ($11.99/month), Oakview rent ($1,550/month), and Harborline Parking ($24.89/month; last listed charge February 5, 2026) are recorded as inventory only. I found no evidence they\u2019re unwanted or erroneous, so I took no action on them.\n- I found no other open fee, duplicate-charge, price-increase, expected-credit, medical-bill, or negotiable-bill leads, and no email deadlines. The records contain only uploaded account history.\n\n**Needed from you:** Whether you had a Peak Wireless unlimited data plan between January 1, 2023 and June 30, 2025.",
